# T2. Any handle press stops a replay mid-way, and the arm holds where it is; the press does nothing else. A
# stopped replay never resumes. Letting go is always possible: the stop lets off the gripper's squeeze (its goal
# is where it is: it may be on a finger), the 30% hold torque stays, and the Pi offers "Let go?" at once.
# The skill is the simulator's made-up sample (src/sim/sampleSkill.ts), SIMULATED, never a taught one.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect 5000 motion command arm.go_to_pose completed operator_cli
key object-left
key skill-run-sample
expect motion target skill.run operator_cli: SIMULATED sample: hold it out
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command skill.run started operator_cli
expect 3000 motion skill grasp left
wait 1500
key t
expect motion command skill.run stopped operator_cli
expect motion stop handle_press
expect motion target gripper.release walker_local: Let go?
expect spoke Let go? Park the walker and lock the brakes, then press Confirm.
absent 500 talk recording
# On the servos: every torqued one holds where it was at the press, within 0.5°, the gripper too (no squeeze), and
# no goal is written in the next second.
wait 200
key inspect-hold-left
expect sim left follower hold ok
absent 1000 sim goal-write left follower
key inspect-hold-tight-left
expect sim left follower hold tight ok (6 servos)
key inspect-grip-left
expect sim left gripper goal-present=0 limit=300
# The person takes it and presses Confirm: only the gripper opens, to the sample's taught angle.
key object-left
wait 2100
key c
expect 3000 motion command gripper.release completed walker_local
expect motion grasp left ended
key q
